{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Build on the Spring XD module model (Java 17 / Spring Framework 6 baseline): implement Kafka source and sink, generator source, and perf-meter sink as deployable XD modules with declarative options metadata.",
    "Kafka source uses the low-level (simple) consumer API to provide deterministic partition assignment and explicit offset control; offsets are tracked externally (ZooKeeper/Kafka offset storage) with handling for broker leader changes and reconnects.",
    "Kafka sink uses the Kafka producer API with configurable encoder/serializer, partitioning strategy, and acknowledgment mode.",
    "Generator source emits synthetic byte-array messages with configurable options numMsgs (default 10000), msgSize (default 1024), and numThreads (default 1), using a thread-safe atomic counter.",
    "Perf-meter sink logs timestamp, cumulative message count, and message rate (messages/second since last log event) to the container log via SLF4J every numMsgs messages (default 1000).",
    "Custom-module installation is exposed as a REST endpoint accepting a multipart uber-jar upload; the server validates the archive, registers it in the module repository/registry, propagates it to containers, and a corresponding xd-shell command is added for the client side.",
    "Test strategy: unit tests with mocks plus integration tests against an embedded Kafka broker, wired into the existing CI build.",
    "Sample reference app is delivered as a standalone GitHub repository with provisioning scripts (e.g., Docker/Vagrant) demonstrating Kafka as message bus and as source."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced developer (familiar with Spring, Spring Integration, Spring XD internals, and Kafka) performs all work; estimates are focused-effort workdays (8 hours), not elapsed time.",
    "A working development environment with the Spring XD codebase, build system, and access to a Kafka broker for development and testing is available or quickly provisioned; an embedded Kafka broker is usable in automated tests.",
    "U1 is a broad epic/vision statement; this increment delivers the Kafka-based ingestion path plus performance tooling as concrete steps toward it. Actual HDFS/HAWQ/GPDB target loaders are out of scope for this increment beyond high-level architecture notes.",
    "U2 is a spike only: research and documentation, no production code; its output feeds the Kafka source implementation.",
    "U3 scope covers server-side REST endpoint, module registry/repository integration, propagation to containers, and a shell command; no web UI is required.",
    "U7 is a measurement/analysis activity using the singlenode container, not a new code deliverable.",
    "Peer/code review effort is included in the final integration activity; documentation targets are READMEs and the project wiki."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Inception, environment setup and architecture design",
      "activity_description": "Set up the development environment (Spring XD build, Kafka broker for dev/test, singlenode container), define module architecture consistent with the XD module model, and outline how the increment supports the mass-ingestion goal of U1.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 spike: study Kafka simple consumer API",
      "activity_description": "Study the Kafka simple (low-level) consumer API covering partition metadata lookup, offset management, leader handling, and fetch requests; build a small throwaway prototype; document findings, recommended approach, and next steps.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Kafka source module implementation (simple consumer API)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Kafka source module based on spike findings: deterministic partition assignment, explicit offset control and persistence, broker/leader failure handling, reconnect logic, configuration options, and basic verification.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Kafka sink module implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Kafka sink module using the producer API with configurable encoder/serializer, partitioning, and acknowledgment settings, plus basic verification.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U3: REST API for custom module (uber-jar) upload and installation",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the REST endpoint for uploading a custom module packaged as an uber-jar, including archive validation, registration in the module repository/registry, propagation to cluster containers, a matching xd-shell command, and API-level tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U4: sample GitHub reference app for XD cluster with Kafka",
      "activity_description": "Create a standalone GitHub sample project with provisioning scripts demonstrating Spring XD with Kafka as message bus and Kafka as source, including stream definitions and README documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U5: generator source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the generator source module producing a configurable number of messages of a specified size across configurable threads (numMsgs/msgSize/numThreads with defaults 10000/1024/1), including unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U6: perf-meter sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the perf-meter sink that logs timestamp, message count, and message rate since the last log event every numMsgs messages (default 1000) to the container log, including unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U7: performance measurement with generator | perf-meter on singlenode",
      "activity_description": "Deploy and run the generator | perf-meter stream on XD's singlenode container ingesting 1M messages of 1000 bytes with one thread, collect throughput/latency characteristics, perform light tuning, and document results.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U8: automated test coverage for Kafka source and sink modules",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests (using an embedded Kafka broker) covering Kafka source and sink functionality, failure/reconnect scenarios, and wire the tests into the CI build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Integration, code review, documentation and release readiness",
      "activity_description": "Integrate all modules, run end-to-end verification, incorporate review feedback, finalize documentation (READMEs/wiki), and prepare the increment for release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 47
  }
}
```

